1
00:00:00,150 --> 00:00:01,741
The sky turns red at sunset

2
00:00:01,741 --> 00:00:02,919
for one simple reason

3
00:00:02,919 --> 00:00:03,460
What is it?

4
00:00:03,660 --> 00:00:04,613
Sunlight looks white

5
00:00:04,613 --> 00:00:05,888
but it's a mix of all colors

6
00:00:05,888 --> 00:00:07,216
from red all the way to blue

7
00:00:07,416 --> 00:00:08,298
When it enters the air

8
00:00:08,298 --> 00:00:10,088
the colors hit tiny air molecules

9
00:00:10,088 --> 00:00:11,661
Blue scatters in every direction

10
00:00:11,661 --> 00:00:12,859
so the sky looks blue

11
00:00:13,059 --> 00:00:13,870
But at sunset

12
00:00:13,870 --> 00:00:15,234
light crosses far more air

13
00:00:15,234 --> 00:00:17,173
Blue scatters away before reaching you

14
00:00:17,373 --> 00:00:18,838
only red and orange remain

15
00:00:18,838 --> 00:00:19,927
painting the sky red

16
00:00:20,127 --> 00:00:21,687
The same air makes both colors

17
00:00:21,687 --> 00:00:23,465
blue at noon, red at sunset!
